Description: privileged mutations of a Frikanalen media archive
 The ingest engine writes into the media archive over SSH. Rather than giving
 the account it logs in as write access to the archive, this package installs
 the two mutations it actually performs -- publish a file, trash a directory --
 as commands that run as the account owning the archive, reached through a
 single sudoers rule.
 .
 Two more ship as operator tools with their own entry points, deliberately
 outside what that rule grants: fk-archive-purge-trash, which is the only thing
 here that deletes anything, and fk-archive-migrate-broadcast, a one-shot
 migration of a video's source out of the directory the previous system kept it
 in.
 .
 Every command validates the paths it is given against the archive's namespace,
 traverses it without following symbolic links, and refuses to overwrite
 anything. Removal is a rename into .trash/.
